.TH SETUP-SYSTEM 1
.SH NAME
setup-system \- manage Debian workstation applications and settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B setup-system
.RB [ \-\-help | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open the Textual interface as the desktop user. Browse the extension catalog,
select a program and review the actions and permissions on its page.
Activating an extension prepares its worker. Choose Install to preview a program
installation. Save profiles independently, preview an individual action, then
confirm its resource changes before Apply.
.PP
Full cleanup previews the exact resources and code recorded for this program.
Review conflicts and preserved user data on the plugin page.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/setup-system/plugins/
Saved plugin profiles. XDG_CONFIG_HOME selects another configuration root.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/setup-system/extensions/
Separate worker environments. XDG_DATA_HOME selects another data root.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/setup-system/
Resource ledger and per-operation history. XDG_STATE_HOME selects another state root.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/setup-system/docs/
Offline administration, configuration and recovery guides.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The normal-user interface accepts declared SETUP_SYSTEM_ preferences for path
completion and worker timeouts. The installed settings_map.md reference gives
their names, units, defaults and limits. Plugin settings belong to the selected
program's Settings and Help tabs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR su (1),
.BR sudo (8)
